ents{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlazos/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":6,"created_at":"2026-02-10T17:36:05Z","updated_at":"2026-03-28T04:02:21Z","closed_at":"2026-03-28T04:02:21Z","assignee":{"login":"mlazos","id":4105940,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMDU5NDA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4105940?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlazos","html_url":"https://github.com/mlazos","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlazos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlazos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlazos/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlazos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlazos/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlazos/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlazos/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlazos/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlazos/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### 🐛 Describe the bug\n\nWhen compiling a function that performs non‑blocking device→host copies followed by a CPU kernel (here: fused cat), Inductor preserves non_blocking=True on the copies but does not insert any wait/barrier before the CPU kernel consumes those pinned CPU buffers. As a result, the CPU kernel can read from buffers whose D2H DMA hasn’t completed yet. The Python‑level torch.Event().record()/synchronize() calls that enforce ordering in eager mode are dropped by Inductor and no alternative synchronization is emitted.\n\n```python\n# repro.py\nimport torch\n\ndef f(a_list):\n    a_cpu_list = []\n    a_to_cpu_event_list = []\n    for a in a_list:\n        # non-blocking D2H\n        a_cpu = a.to(device=\"cpu\", non_blocking=True)\n        # explicit event ordering in eager\n        e = torch.Event()\n        e.record()\n        a_cpu_list.append(a_cpu)\n        a_to_cpu_event_list.append(e)\n\n    # ensure all D2H have finished before CPU consumption\n    for e in a_to_cpu_event_list:\n        e.synchronize()\n\n    return torch.cat(a_cpu_list)\n\ndef main():\n    f_compiled = torch.compile(f)  # default Inductor backend\n    inputs = [torch.rand(1000, dtype=torch.float16, device=\"cuda\") for _ in range(100)]\n    out = f_compiled(inputs)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\nEnabling TORCH_COMPILE_DEBUG=1 and running the script produces code (shortened) like:\n```python\nbuf0 = empty_strided_cpu_pinned((1000,), (1,), torch.float16)\nbuf0.copy_(arg0_1, True)   # non_blocking=True is preserved\n\n# ... repeated for buf1..buf99 ...\n\n# fused CPU kernel immediately consumes buf0..buf99\ncpp_fused_cat_0(buf0, buf1, ..., buf99, buf100, ..., buf199)\n```\n\nPreserving the non_blocking attribute was added by https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/pull/136513.\n\nThe reproducer is taken from the pytorch unit test [here](https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/947729b8be8d33d45fe613e0f14885a55fbc2dba/test/inductor/test_torchinductor.py#L14852-L14896).  The test is flaky, and was skipped on ROCm Navi because it was frequently observed to fail there.  But this is a generic issue.\n\n### Versions\n\nCC @eellison @NiklasZ \n\ncc @ezyang @gchanan @kadeng @msaroufim @chauhang @penguinwu @voznesenskym @EikanWang @jgong5 @Guobing-Chen @XiaobingSuper @zhuhaozhe @blzheng @wenzhe-nrv @jiayisunx @ipiszy @muchulee8 @amjames @aakhundov @coconutruben @jataylo","closed_by":{"login":"mlazos","id":4105940,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMDU5NDA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4105940?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlazos","html_url":"https://github.com/mlazos","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlazos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlazos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlazos/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlazos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlazos/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlazos/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlazos/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlazos/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlazos/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/174695/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/174695/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}